ntly-verified verdict) |
 
+## Focused-task selector audit (campaign 45195964697, agent 01, task P-001)
+
+**Question:** Does the current focused-task selector improve learning efficiency relative to the prior opportunistic task choice?
+
+**Decision: RETAIN (no demonstrated advantage; two verified defects logged as P-007/P-008).** The selector (`campaign_controller.py:206-225`, `307-311`) is a deterministic lexicographic ordering over seven static queue attributes plus `task_id`, restricted to OPEN tasks of the agent's role. That is traceable and role-scoped and removes queue-position choice, but it is not linked to this frontier: no controller path reads `state/LEARNING_STATE.md` (only `synthesize_campaign.py:210` references it, for synthesis). The frontier's declared Next (line 13, cost test = R-001) is selected only because the queue metadata happens to rank R-001 first among OPEN research tasks.
+
+**Verified defects (not repaired here; `.github/scripts/**` is outside the campaign write scope):**
+
+1. `selection_basis.qualitative_priority` (`campaign_controller.py:339-351`) is the selected task's own seven attribute values, while `compared_against` is up to five candidate task_ids including the selected task. No per-candidate ranks are computed or stored, so the record cannot substantiate "highest priority" (agent_01_contract.json shows five ids against seven priorities).
+2. Queue status is not reconciled with artifacts. `research/checks/momentum_hold_period_sensitivity.py` is a complete R-002 check that writes `state/check_artifacts/momentum_hold_period_sensitivity_results.json`, but that artifact and any R-002 verdict are absent while `task_queue.json` still lists R-002 OPEN. A status-only selector cannot distinguish partially executed work from untouched work.
+3. No test covers selection_basis semantics, per-candidate ranking, or queue-to-artifact freshness.
+
+**Outcome history:** six post-adoption cells (mean-reversion, cross-sectional relative strength, volatility targeting, momentum, momentum lookback/longer-horizon, breakout) each closed with one decisive verdict and independent verification, with no equivalent re-tests. Five of the seven cells are momentum-family qualifications (six momentum check scripts plus cross-sectional momentum among 30 check scripts). This is consistent with a working process but cannot be attributed to the selector: the opportunistic period has one documented selection instance (37260572520, objective from a queued receipt item) and no per-activation information-gain measurement.
+
+**Unverified:** the causal efficiency claim (no pre-adoption baseline); controller-side validation of this record; whether the five-versus-seven mismatch already misled a downstream agent.
+
+**Next:** P-007 (reconstruct the pre-adoption information-gain baseline under one fixed rubric) before any selector change; P-008 (task-to-artifact coverage matrix) to expose partially executed queue work.
+
 ## Learning rules
 
 1. One substantive activation should normally choose one primary strategy delta.
 2. A repeated experiment requires a new hypothesis, diagnostic purpose, materially new data, independent verification need, or different information objective.

